1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,862
Ringing that shows up after time at the range, a few vapes, or just getting older?

2
00:00:04,182 --> 00:00:09,327
Loud shots, nicotine, and a common vitamin gap can each trigger tinnitus in very different ways.

3
00:00:09,647 --> 00:00:17,678
A single gunshot can hit 150 to 165 decibels, past the one-shot limit NIOSH sets at 140.

4
00:00:17,998 --> 00:00:22,662
That much noise can damage the inner ear instantly, and ringing is often the first sign.

5
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:27,125
Nicotine in vapes narrows the tiny blood vessels feeding the inner ear.

6
00:00:27,445 --> 00:00:34,047
Less oxygen reaching those cells is linked to new or worse tinnitus, especially with frequent e-cigarette use.

7
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:37,641
Low vitamin B12 can wear down the nerves in the inner ear.

8
00:00:37,961 --> 00:00:46,006
One study found nearly half of people with noise-related hearing loss and tinnitus were low on B12, especially those eating little meat or dairy.

9
00:00:46,326 --> 00:00:48,919
Wear earplugs around gunfire or loud equipment.

10
00:00:49,239 --> 00:00:57,605
If vaping is a daily habit, cutting back - even by half - may ease the strain on inner-ear blood flow, and a doctor can help if quitting feels hard.

11
00:00:57,925 --> 00:01:02,816
And if your diet is light on meat and dairy, ask about a B12 test or fortified supplement.
